+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for small businesses in 2026?
+For most teams, the strongest starting points are Dify, Langflow, Flowise, Open WebUI, AnythingLLM, RAGFlow, Chatwoot, and CrewAI. The right pick depends on whether you need workflow automation, internal chat, document search, customer support, or agent orchestration.
+
+### Which self-hosted AI tool is best for a small business knowledge base?
+AnythingLLM, DocsGPT, RAGFlow, FastGPT, and Open WebUI are the most practical options here. If you need a polished employee-facing chat workspace, start with AnythingLLM or Open WebUI. If you care more about retrieval fidelity and document pipelines, start with RAGFlow or Haystack.
+
+### Are there free AI customer support tools on GitHub for small businesses?
+Yes. Chatwoot, Rasa, Botpress, and OpenAssistantGPT all have public GitHub repositories and can be self-hosted. Chatwoot is the most complete support-desk option, while Rasa and Botpress are stronger if you need more custom conversational logic.
+
+### What is the best open source AI workflow automation alternative to Zapier for small businesses?
+n8n and Activepieces are the most obvious workflow-first choices, while Dify, Langflow, and Flowise become better picks once the workflow itself is heavily AI-driven. If your process starts with forms, tickets, spreadsheets, and APIs, begin with n8n or Activepieces.
+
+### Which GitHub AI repos are best for building internal company copilots?
+Dify, Open WebUI, AnythingLLM, Lobe Chat, Khoj, DocsGPT, and Haystack are the best candidates from this list. They give you different tradeoffs across user experience, retrieval depth, infrastructure control, and engineering flexibility.
+
+### Are all tools in this list public GitHub repositories?
+Yes. Every entry links to a public `github.com` repository. Closed SaaS-only products were excluded, even when they are popular in the small-business market.
+
+### Did any categories come up short during research?
+Yes. Pure-play open source AI products aimed specifically at accounting, invoicing, or SMB bookkeeping are still thinner than workflow, support, and knowledge-assistant categories. That gap is real, so this list broadens the scope to “AI tools useful to small businesses” rather than pretending there are dozens of mature accounting-native GitHub projects already.
